---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/holiday-gifting';
const title = "Recover gift orders with honest fulfillment choices";
const desc = "Gift shoppers need to know whether the intended item can reach the intended recipient. Build recovery around the destination, fulfillment method and gift promise rather than a fixed number of weeks before a holiday.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">{desc}</p>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-12">
      <h2>Make deadlines operational</h2>
      <p>Have fulfillment staff approve destination-specific order cutoffs with timezone, processing time and carrier service. Treat these as planning estimates unless an actual guarantee applies. Recheck the landing page and message when a cutoff changes; queued copy must not retain an obsolete arrival promise.</p>
      <h2>Keep gift details intact</h2>
      <p>Preserve gift wrapping, recipient address, gift note and bundle contents where the checkout supports them. Confirm whether prices appear in packaging and how returns work for the recipient. Avoid exposing a personal gift note in the subject or preview text, especially for shared inboxes.</p>
      <h2>Branch after physical delivery closes</h2>
      <p>Offer pickup, another supported shipping service or a digital gift option only when it is actually available for that destination and product. Explain the difference between placing an order and receiving a digital code. Do not substitute a gift card for a physical gift without the shopper choosing it.</p>
      <h2>Handle split and changing inventory</h2>
      <p>If a bundle contains unavailable items, state whether it can ship partially and whether the recipient will receive separate parcels. Suppress a recovery promise that the warehouse cannot fulfill. Route uncertain personalized production dates to support before encouraging an urgent purchase.</p>
      <h2>Proposed rehearsal</h2>
      <p>Create a gift basket with a note, a bundle and a destination beyond the cutoff. Inspect both the recovery message and checkout after the deadline passes. Review late-arrival contacts, cancellations and contribution alongside recovered orders. A sale-calendar result does not establish whether recipients received gifts in time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
